cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Criticality Spectrometer"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Brandes
    given-names: Amadeus
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-14"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AMBRA7592/criticality-spectrometer"
abstract: >-
  A domain-agnostic instrument for measuring how the impact of removing a node
  changes as alternatives become available over an adaptation horizon, in
  systems with typed AND/OR dependencies. Criticality is represented as a
  response curve over adaptation time rather than a scalar ranking, separating
  path redundancy from capability-preserving redundancy.
keywords:
  - dependency analysis
  - criticality
  - substitutability
  - supply chain resilience
  - network analysis
